  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Technical Assistance Facility to Support Sustainable Infrastructure Development in South Africa</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&lt;p&gt;The purpose of this contract is provision of technical assistance to improve policy and regulatory environment and institutional framework for stimulation of innovative technical and financing models for sustainable infrastructure development within all three spheres of government in South Africa &#xbf; national, provincial and local. The contractor is deliver practical and effective technical assistance to support the realisation of three main Expected Outputs of the programme (EO) 1 &#xbf; 3.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;EO 1: Improved policy, strategy and regulatory framework, including the analytical &#xbf; evidence base for sustainable infrastructure delivery;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;EO 2: Enhanced capacities, training programmes and expertise resources for evidence-based planning and implementation of innovative financing strategies and environmentally friendly, sustainable and resilient infrastructure;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;EO 3: Improved coordination, planning, implementation and accountability mechanisms for infrastructure delivery and alignment with NDP and Agenda 2030.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Beneficiaries will include the South African authorities, notably National Treasury of South Africa, other infrastructure stakeholders at national, provincial and local levels of the government. The activities will also include private sector organisations, civil society organisations and community-based organisations.&lt;/p&gt;</narrative>
  </description>
